From 06d6fcd78d9b51594a60b33ef611e010d774b0e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: utzcoz <utzcoz@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:02:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] webxr: support frame rate control with OpenXR

XRSession.frameRate, supportedFrameRates and updateTargetFrameRate were
stubs that reported no frame rate. Back them with
XR_FB_display_refresh_rate, which Meta Link, Monado and others expose.

The device reports the supported rates and the current rate when the
session starts, and the current rate with every frame, so a change made
by the runtime reaches the page too. A new optional
XRFrameRateController interface forwards the page's target rate to the
runtime; the device rejects rates it did not offer. Blink follows the
spec's updateTargetFrameRate steps and fires frameratechange when the
rate in the frame data changes.

Runtimes without the extension behave as before: both attributes stay
null.

The WebXR Test API cannot set up frame rates, so the web tests extend
the Chromium mock in wpt_internal.

Bug: 506004811
Change-Id: Ie8f902973efb65fa4bce922180a271172aaa085d
